{{Quote|A time will come, decades from now, when the ships of the Mon Calamari are at the forefront of a great rebellion. And then, again, decades after that. Your people's vessels will be a symbol of freedom and defiance across the galaxy. And it all started here, Your Majesty. With you.|[[Ferren Barr]], to [[King]] [[Lee-Char]] during the [[invasion of Mon Cala]]|<ref name="Dark Lord 17">[[Darth Vader (2017) 17|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 17]]</ref>}}
The '''MC80 Star Cruisers''',<ref name="Manual">''[[YT-1300 Millennium Falcon Owners' Workshop Manual]]''</ref> were [[capital ship]]s used by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. These immense vessels were a startling contrast to the angular-shaped [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyers]], which were favored by the [[Imperial Navy|Imperial Fleet]]. Whereas the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[warship]] resembled a pointed dagger in shape, a Mon Calamari cruiser lacked hard angles and was covered with ovoid forms suggesting an organic sculpture. There were pods attached all around the ship, containing turbolasers, sensor arrays and viewing ports, the latter fulfilling the ships' original intended role as an exploration and observation vessel. Each [[cruiser]] was of a unique design.<ref name="UltimateSW" /> Despite their smooth lines, these vessels were heavily armed with dozens of [[turbolaser]]s, [[SW-7 ion cannon]]s,<ref name="EHWaUE">{{EncyclopediaCite|Explosives, Heavy Weapons, and Power Sources}}</ref> [[tractor beam]] projectors and [[Deflector shield generator|shield generators]].<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|mon-calamari-star-cruiser|Mon Calamari star cruiser}}</ref> The [[MC80A Home One Type Heavy Star Cruiser|MC80A ''Home One'' Type Heavy Star Cruiser]] was a variant of the MC80 star cruiser.<ref name="Starfighters">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref>

==History==
===Early rebellion===
The MC80 Star Cruiser line was an important part of the [[Galactic Civil War]], being the backbone of the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]]. The first known use of the ship was in the year [[18 BBY]] during the [[Invasion of Mon Cala]]. There, a group of MC80A and MC75 star cruisers led by [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] and [[Commander]] [[Gial Ackbar]] broke free of the Imperial blockade and escaped into the galaxy.<ref name="Dark Lord 17" />

===Alliance to Restore the Republic===
[[File:MonCalamariCruiser-TSWB.png|thumb|left|300px|A MC80A ''Home One'' Type Heavy Star Cruiser]]
During the formation of the Alliance to Restore the Republic, the [[MC80A Home One Type Heavy Star Cruiser|MC80A cruiser]] ''[[Home One]]'' was present and joined the Alliance fleet.<ref name="Secret Cargo">{{Rebels|Secret Cargo}}</ref>

After the execution of king [[Lee-Char]] was broadcasted across [[Mon Cala]], in which he was killed by [[stormtrooper]]s, the crew of the [[Mon Cala Mercantile Fleet]] began to rebel. With the help of the Alliance, the fleet escaped the Imperial blockade and retreated with the Alliance.<ref name="SW 49">[[Star Wars (2015) 49|''Star Wars'' (2015) 49]]</ref> The fleet, consisting of twelve ''Liberty'' types and two MC80A cruisers, along with other Mon Cala cruisers like the [[MC75 Star Cruiser]], arrived at the [[Mako-Ta Space Docks]] to be retrofitted to become full-fledged warships.<ref name="Star Wars 50">[[Star Wars (2015) 50|''Star Wars'' (2015) 50]]</ref> However, this was a trap and [[Death Squadron]] arrived to destroy the fleet. The rebels were able to escape, but only after most of their ships were destroyed.<ref name="SW 55">[[Star Wars (2015) 55|''Star Wars'' (2015) 55]]</ref>

Several of these warships participated in the decisive [[Battle of Endor]]. There, ships such as the ''[[Liberty]]'' and ''Home One'' helped defeat the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]] and destroy the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]].<ref name="Episode VI" />

===New Republic service===
Shortly after the Battle of Endor, the Alliance transformed into the [[New Republic]], with the MC80 line continuing to be used within the [[New Republic Defense Fleet]], participating in battles across the galaxy on planets such as [[Attack on Fondor|Fondor]],<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> [[Battle of Theed|Naboo]],<ref name="Shattered Empire 3">[[Shattered Empire 3|''Shattered Empire'' 3]]</ref> [[Defense of Kuat|Kuat]],<ref name="Blade Squadron: Kuat">{{InsiderCite|168|Blade Squadron: Kuat}}</ref> and [[Liberation of Kashyyyk|Kashyyyk]].<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> Many MC80 star cruisers, including both the MC80A and ''Liberty'' type, participated in the [[Battle of Jakku]]. There, forces led by Ackbar on the ''Home One'' defeated the Imperial fleet, winning the Galactic Civil War.<ref name="Battlefront II" />

===Resistance service===
Eventually, ''Home One'' was retired from service in the New Republic fleet and was used by the Resistance.<ref name="BTA">''[[Before the Awakening]]''</ref> In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="TROS Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] to one [[Standard year|year]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. As ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of ''The Force Awakens'' to [[34 ABY]], the events of ''The Rise of Skywalker'' must occur in [[35 ABY]].</ref> MC80 Star Cruisers were part of a [[Citizens' Fleet|fleet]] assembled by [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] to assist the Resistance during the [[Battle of Exegol|battle]] against the [[Sith Eternal military|Sith Eternal forces]] over the [[planet]] [[Exegol]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

